the top commander of the palestinian  armed group and the al-aqsa brigades has  been killed in a raid by israeli forces  in the occupied west bank ibrahim  nabulsi was known as the lion of nablus  there are reports that others were also  killed in the operation palestinian  authorities say more than 30 people were  wounded  well john holman joins us on the phone  now he's on the road to where this  happened  john what more do we know about the raid  at this point in time  yeah we know that it happened or it  began at around 5 a.m uh so early in the  morning  when israeli forces entered into the  occupied west bank  and they went to the old city in nablus  which is  a sort of a place it's as its name  described it's old and it's got  buildings that are quite close together  they surrounded the building uh in which  uh ibrahim al-nabusi had sort of hold  himself up and then there was a  firefight which according to our  colleagues our producers  in uh in the occupied west bank lasted  for hours and during that time he  refused to surrender and he was defended  by other armed palestinians eventually  the israeli forces the israeli military  uh managed to manage to kill him it's  actually uh unusual that that sort of  raid would happen at that time during  the daylight hours usually they happen  uh in the night time when obviously  there's less civilians  sort of around and as you mentioned uh  there were more than 30 people injured  four of those in a critical condition so  the sort of the result of having this  firefight possibly at this time and in  that crowded uh area um now uh  ibrahimowski  was a commander of the al-aqsa martyrs  brigade which is the military arm of the  fatah uh political movement uh  just for our audience who will obviously  have been following what's been  happening in gaza over the last few days  that's separate from islamic jihad which  is another uh palestinian group of uh  resistance that's operating in the  occupied west bank but also in gaza so  this is a separate this is a separate  sort of attack on a separate uh force  that's in the occupied west bank we also  know as well that this wasn't the first  time that israeli forces had had tried  to get uh ibrahim al-nabul they tried  several times including in july in a  massive operation again in which two  other men died  john holman thank you very much for that  update
 

